<title>THAILAND: THAI FINMIN SAYS NO MORE TROUBLED FINANCIAL FIRMS.</title>
<headline>THAI FINMIN SAYS NO MORE TROUBLED FINANCIAL FIRMS.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya tried to calm panicked depositors after the susupension of ailing 42 finance firms by reiterating on Wednesday the government will not let remaining financial insitutions to go under.</p>
<p>Thanong told reporters after a meeting with top exectives of Thailand's five largest commercial banks the government has set up a plan and mechanism to save smaller banks and remaining financial firms from collapsing from a deposit run.</p>
</text>
